{
  "_comment": "Time zones of the world pack: a curated dataset (CC BY 4.0, see datasets/LICENSE.md). packbuild.timezones turns it into the world pack's `timezones` polygon layer. `countries` has one entry per unit of the world pack's countries layer (Natural Earth admin-0, ids iso:XX or ne:XXX): an IANA zone name for a country with one zone, null where tzdb records no zone (the nearest-city rule answers), or an object with `zone` (the whole country, or the rest of it when `admin1` lists exceptions) and `admin1` (Natural Earth admin-1 ids -> zone; without `zone` every admin-1 unit of the country is listed). A zone can be a list: the unit is split along lines Natural Earth doesn't draw, the first entry is its main zone and the nearest city inside the unit whose zone is listed decides. `shapes` are hand-drawn areas (boxes as [south, west, north, east], or a polygon of [lat, lon] points) that take precedence inside the unit named by `within`. Every zone must exist in the tz database; `sources` name entries of the top-level `sources`.",
